Exact operator identities
-------------------------
Starting from H/V=(1/2)a_dagger^2 a^2+delta a_dagger a+
eta(a_dagger+a), direct normal ordering after a=b-r and
r^3+delta*r=eta gives

 H/V=-3r^4/2-delta*r^2+(2r^2+delta)b_dagger b
     +(r^2/2)(b_dagger^2+b^2)
     -r(b_dagger^2 b+b_dagger b^2)+(1/2)b_dagger^2 b^2.

The linear terms vanish exactly.  The real Bogoliubov transformation obeys

 tanh(2 theta)=-r^2/(2r^2+delta),
 Omega^2=(2r^2+delta)^2-r^4.

Formal perturbative result through order one
--------------------------------------------
At leading order, C^2+S^2=2/sqrt(3) and 2CS=-1/sqrt(3).  Exact symbolic
ladder action, not matrix diagonalization, gives

 Delta4_n =
 [18n^2+(18-16sqrt(3))n+15-8sqrt(3)]/24,

 Delta3_n =
 -[30n^2+(30-24sqrt(3))n+23-12sqrt(3)]/36,

 Delta4_n+Delta3_n=-(6n^2+6n+1)/72.

The first-order cubic term vanishes by parity.  The first-order quartic and
second-order cubic terms both contribute at order one.

The stationarity solution used is

 r=eta^(1/3)-(delta/3)eta^(-1/3)
   +(delta^3/81)eta^(-5/3)+O(eta^(-7/3)).

The exact quadratic energy contributes delta(1-2delta)/6 at order one.
Therefore, for fixed n, formal Rayleigh--Schrodinger perturbation theory gives

 E_n/V=-3eta^(4/3)/2
 +[delta+sqrt(3)(n+1/2)-1]eta^(2/3)
 +delta(1-2delta)/6-(6n^2+6n+1)/72
 +O(eta^(-2/3)).

This confirms the candidate coefficient.  It is an independently verified
formal operator asymptotic, not a theorem about the unresolved global Olver
connection and not accompanied by a rigorous perturbative remainder bound.

The corresponding formal differences are

 (E_(n+1)-E_n)/V=sqrt(3)eta^(2/3)-(n+1)/6+O(eta^(-2/3)),
 (E_(n+2)-2E_(n+1)+E_n)/V=-1/6+O(eta^(-2/3)).

Status of the eta^(-2/3) coefficient
------------------------------------
UNFINISHED; no coefficient was guessed.

The completed exact quadratic contribution is

 delta^3/27+sqrt(3)delta^2 n/18-delta^2/9
 +sqrt(3)delta^2/36.

Still required are finite-r corrections to the first-order quartic term and
second-order cubic vertices/denominators, second-order V4^2, normalized
third-order V3^2 V4, and normalized fourth-order V3^4.  Odd total cubic
parity vanishes.

The manuscript and report record the exact remaining finite sum.  With
X_jk=<j|V3/r|k>, Y_jk=<j|V4|k>, D_k=sqrt(3)(n-k), it consists of

 sum Y_nk Y_kn/D_k,
 sum (X_nk X_kl Y_ln+X_nk Y_kl X_ln+Y_nk X_kl X_ln)/(D_k D_l),
 -Y_nn sum X_nk X_kn/D_k^2,
 sum X_nk X_kl X_lm X_mn/(D_k D_l D_m),
 -(sum X_nk X_kn/D_k)(sum X_nl X_ln/D_l^2),

with all intermediate indices unequal to n.  X has shifts +/-1,+/-3 and Y
has shifts 0,+/-2,+/-4, so every sum terminates.  Evaluation and combination
with finite-r derivatives is the smallest remaining algebraic task.

Complete pullback and endpoint cancellation
--------------------------------------------
The manuscript now uses neutral W1,W2 labels.  The complete exact pullback is

 Psi(z)=t^(1/2-B2) exp[B1/(2t^2)]
        (d zeta/dx)^(-1/2) W(zeta(x)),

 z=t^2, t=eta^(1/6)x, B1=2eta, B2=2delta.

Using

 u integral^x sqrt(Q_u) ds=-u/x^2-2(1-delta)log(x)+O(1),
 zeta~+/-i sqrt(2)/x, (d zeta/dx)^(-1/2)~constant*x,

the neutral endpoint pair can be normalized as

 W1~x^(-3/2+2delta)exp(-u/x^2),
 W2~x^(5/2-2delta)exp(+u/x^2).

Direct multiplication proves at the formal endpoint level

 T_u W1~1,
 T_u W2~x^(4-4delta)exp(2u/x^2)
       ~z^(2-2delta)exp(2eta/z).

A generic combination therefore retains

 Psi~C1[1+...]+C_ess z^(2-2delta)exp(2eta/z)[1+...].

Branch reversal exchanges W1 and W2 but preserves the invariant
cancellation/enhancement distinction.  Local cancellation is not global
patching, and Stokes continuation can restore the essential component.

Connection conjecture
----------------------
The manuscript contains a numbered and explicitly labelled conjecture.
For normalized initial and terminal bases and conjectural continuation
A_Gamma,

 A_Gamma W1^(0)=C1 W1^(m)+C_ess W2^(m),

 C_ess=
 Wronskian_zeta(A_Gamma W1^(0),W1^(m))/
 Wronskian_zeta(W2^(m),W1^(m)).

Bilinearity verifies the sign because numerator and denominator use the same
Wronskian order.  Nonzero basis renormalizations change C_ess only by a
nonzero factor.

The existence of the domain chain, sectorial solutions and continuation,
symmetry reduction to C_ess=0, equivalence to holomorphic patching, equality
of zero sets with Delta_WI, local factorization C_ess=G Delta_WI, and the
expected form

 C_ess=A/Gamma[-p_u(E)]+R, A nonzero, R=O(u^-1 A)

are all explicitly conjectural.  The exact Delta_WI determinant remains an
independent theorem.  No continued fraction was used.

